% The second cook's domain, served on its own (RACK.md §5, rack step 1):
% the shared kitchen as the second cook sees it — its own orders, its
% own pot recipe (kitchen.llp), and one move more: dropping an onion it
% holds into the FIRST cook's pot (partner_load). On this tape that move
% is an event; on the first cook's tape (catalogs/kitchen_host.llp) the
% extra onion is a surprise, explained by the kitchen_shared card.
% In its own folder so the first cook's cards op does not list it twice.
catalog kitchen_shared 1.
provenance text "a shared kitchen: a second cook also loads onions into the pot" "2026-10-12".
include "../kitchen.llp".
weight w_partner.
stage task {
  %% the second cook drops the onion it holds into the first cook's pot.
  %% target: kitchen
  partner_load [task] : held_onion -o hand_free  @w w_partner.
}
#init hand_free 1
#query served
#query cooking
#query held_soup
#steps 12
